there's an option for you.

00:47:17.140 --> 00:47:19.900
And also, because it's a
fully managed service--

00:47:19.900 --> 00:47:21.790
and I like to stress this--

00:47:21.790 --> 00:47:23.930
you don't have to
worry about a anything

00:47:23.930 --> 00:47:25.520
around your key management.

00:47:25.520 --> 00:47:26.020
Sorry.

00:47:26.020 --> 00:47:28.061
You only have to worry
about your key management,

00:47:28.061 --> 00:47:30.710
not around your HSM management.

00:47:30.710 --> 00:47:33.370
And finally, you can now
actually go and use it

00:47:33.370 --> 00:47:34.871
for a lot more things.

00:47:34.871 --> 00:47:37.120
You have that CA that you
want to move up to the cloud

00:47:37.120 --> 00:47:38.911
because you want it
close to your workload?

00:47:38.911 --> 00:47:39.880
Now you can do it.

00:47:39.880 --> 00:47:42.440
So it's all possible for you.

00:47:42.440 --> 00:47:44.540
And with that, I
think we're done.

00:47:44.540 --> 00:47:47.237
We have a couple of minutes
